NOTICE: the PropBank frames annex
=================================

What this directory is
----------------------
frames/ holds 24 frameset files in PropBank format. Each defines one relational-noun roleset, for example mom.01
("ARG1 is a parent of ARG0"). memory-kernel reads them together with the upstream PropBank frames (see
memory_kernel.pipeline.frames); none of the 24 roleset ids exists upstream, so nothing here replaces an upstream roleset.

Upstream work these files build on
----------------------------------
PropBank frames, https://github.com/propbank/propbank-frames, at commit c66e0ccf28b53f00051b187db83e937b5bee2e32 (the
commit `mk setup` fetches), by the contributors to propbank/propbank-frames
(https://github.com/propbank/propbank-frames/graphs/contributors). The PropBank project site, https://propbank.github.io/,
states: "This work is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License" and "Propbank
annotation is done at CLEAR under the supervision of Martha Palmer". Licence:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode (a byte copy of the upstream LICENSE is in this directory). No
copyright notice is supplied upstream. The frameset file format, the DTD, the roleset naming scheme (<lemma>.<nn>) and the
role labels (ARG0, ARG1, ...) follow it.

Changes made (adaptations)
--------------------------
Eight files add one roleset to a lemma that upstream already defines, in an upstream file of the same name. Each holds only
the added roleset, not the lemma's upstream rolesets:

    buddy.xml     buddy.02       mentor.xml    mentor.02
    father.xml    father.02      mother.xml    mother.02
    friend.xml    friend.02      neighbor.xml  neighbor.02
    kid.xml       kid.02         partner.xml   partner.02

Sixteen files define a lemma that upstream has no file for. They are original to this package:

    bestie, boyfriend, brother, colleague, coworker, dad, daughter, family,
    girlfriend, husband, mom, pal, roommate, sister, son, wife   (each .xml, each .01)

